<HeroTag text="Independent Review · July 2026" />
<h1>OLSP System Review: What It Is, How It Works, and Whether It's Worth It</h1>

<p><strong>The OLSP System</strong> is a bundled affiliate-marketing platform created by Wayne Crowe and launched around 2020. It combines training, prospecting tools, a pre-built sales funnel, and a two-tier commission structure into a single membership. The question most people searching for a review actually want answered is simple: is the OLSP System a worthwhile use of time and money, or is it a recruitment-driven program dressed up as an education platform?</p>

<p>Our short answer, based on independent desk research of public materials and third-party commentary: the OLSP System can work as a low-cost introduction to affiliate marketing for people comfortable with promoting a recruitment-based model, but it shares structural characteristics with multi-level marketing programs, and most publicly circulating income claims are self-reported and unverifiable.</p>

<VerdictBox>
<p><strong>Best for:</strong> beginners who want a guided, done-for-you introduction to affiliate marketing and are comfortable with a model where most income comes from getting others to join and upgrade — not from selling stand-alone products to one-time customers.</p>
<p><strong>Not ideal for:</strong> anyone looking for passive income, anyone uncomfortable with an upsell-and-recruit driven structure, or anyone who would prefer to build an independent, owned audience they control outside a single vendor's ecosystem.</p>
</VerdictBox>

<Methodology>
<p><strong>How this review was built:</strong> We did not purchase, join, or personally test the OLSP System. This review is based on independent desk research: the program's public marketing pages, third-party commentary, and general consumer-protection context for affiliate and income-opportunity programs. Where a claim could not be independently verified — including most income figures — we say so explicitly.</p>
</Methodology>
</section>

<section id="tools">
<h2>What the OLSP System Includes</h2>

<p>The OLSP System is broader than the OLSP Academy training layer that often dominates the marketing materials. Understanding the full scope helps assess whether the total value justifies joining at any tier.</p>

<h3>Core Components</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>OLSP Academy:</strong> the training and onboarding layer — short video lessons (Bootcamp), live webinars, and a Facebook-based community for members. This is the educational component of the system.</li>
<li><strong>Mega Link:</strong> a single, trackable referral link that members share instead of building their own website or sales page. Every other component of the system funnels prospects toward this link.</li>
<li><strong>Mega Funnel:</strong> the automated follow-up sequence that runs on the member's behalf after someone clicks their link — email sequences, webinar replays, and Facebook Live events that handle the selling.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Optional Paid Add-Ons</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>VIP / Accelerator:</strong> a higher-priced coaching tier (reported around $97/month) with extended training, higher commission rates, and access to additional marketing assets. Commission payouts for VIP referrals are cited at $150–$300 per conversion in third-party materials.</li>
<li><strong>TD Pages:</strong> a landing-page builder sold as a separate tool.</li>
<li><strong>Solo Ads / Traffic Packages:</strong> paid traffic services sending visitors to a member's link — separate purchases, not included in the base membership.</li>
<li><strong>LeadsMiner Pro &amp; MineeMe:</strong> Facebook prospecting and engagement tools for identifying leads and increasing organic visibility.</li>
</ul>

<Callout type="info">
<strong>What's included vs. what costs extra:</strong> Public pricing information varies across sources. The free tier reportedly gives access to the core Academy training and a Mega Link. Nearly everything else — VIP coaching, traffic services, prospecting tools — is a separate purchase. Verify current pricing directly on the official sign-up page before assuming anything is included.
</Callout>
</section>

