<p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--ink-light);margin-top:-.3rem;">Editorial scores reflect our own assessment based on the research described in this article — not a certification, lab test, or audited rating.</p>

<p>The OLSP System is a genuinely low-friction way for a complete beginner to experience what affiliate marketing involves — sharing a link, driving traffic, and earning commissions when people buy. The structured training and active community are real assets. The honest caveat is that the system's two-tier commission structure rewards recruitment more than product sales, most income claims are unverifiable, and the long list of paid add-ons creates structural pressure to keep spending. If you join, treat it as a practical learning experience with a low entry cost — not a guaranteed path to income. The people likeliest to see results are those who treat consistent traffic generation as a daily practice and are comfortable promoting a recruitment-based model.</p>

